cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spatialTXsuite in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "spatialTXsuite: an R Shiny application for replicate-aware spatial transcriptomics analysis"
abstract: >-
  spatialTXsuite is an R Shiny application for interactive analysis of
  spatial transcriptomics data stored as SpatialExperiment objects. It imports
  10x Visium (Space Ranger folders or GEO-style count and position files),
  Xenium, MERFISH and CosMx data, alone or from a multi-section sample sheet.
  The workflow covers platform-aware quality control, normalisation, joint
  spatial domain detection shared across sections (Harmony-corrected
  expression with within-section neighbourhood smoothing), per-section spatial
  autocorrelation (Moran's I and Geary's C), and pseudobulk differential
  expression with edgeR quasi-likelihood tests. Differential expression is
  replicate-aware: sections from the same animal or donor can be pooled, likely
  pseudoreplication is flagged, technical covariates such as Visium slide can
  be adjusted for, and the reference condition is explicit.
authors:
